{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": "Render SHA256 and open finding counts per surface and cell (theme-viewport-state). Populated by the admin-eval harness (Plan 07). Each guard reads this as the single authoritative source for render_sha256 and open_findings — render-sha and open-finding counts are consolidated here so quality-findings-monotonic.sh has one stable file to diff. Schema documented in guides/reference/admin-eval-schema.md. Cell render_sha256 values are computed from board outerHTML via renderSha256() in canonicalize.ts. For users-index-live, primary evidence board is board-mg-5 (user-results-pagination). For user-show-live, primary evidence board is board-mg-9 (identity-header-summary-facts). open_findings = total probe findings minus settled entries in settled-findings.tsv. Plan 217-08 (Option 2): board-mg-5-* and board-mg-9-* surfaces added so the LLM panel targets the same concrete boards the render matrix actually renders. open_findings set to 0 (gate-safe: panel reads only render_sha256). Phase 218-01 (D-02): full matrix expansion — all 11 L2 boards (4 states each), 13 L1 boards (single -default state), and 8 L3 surfaces (2 pilots + 6 net-new proxies with proxy:true flag). L3 proxy surfaces reuse their representative board's render_sha256 byte-identically. fix-queue-build.mjs structurally skips proxy:true surfaces in step (j) so builder runs cannot clobber pinned open_findings. L2/L1 boards with render_sha256 = '0000...000' have not yet been captured by the eval harness (Plan 218-02 will capture them and update via fix-queue-build.mjs). L3 proxy mapping: index-live=board-mg-1, organization-live=board-mg-7, users-index-live=board-mg-5(pilot), user-show-live=board-mg-9(pilot), user-sessions=board-mg-11, audit-index-live=board-mg-6, audit-user-live=board-mg-6, branding-live=board-mg-4.",
